	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - System - Session - Okta Admin Console Accessed",
	"Description": "Someone opened the Okta admin console. Compare the actor, the source address, and the geolocation against who is supposed to be administering the org; admin console access from an unexpected address or country is worth chasing even when the credentials were valid.\n\nEvent types: user.session.access_admin_app, plus any request whose URI is under /admin\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
